# Project Rules

**Cloud MVP (current):** start at [`docs/ARCHITECTURE_CLOUD.md`](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE_CLOUD.md) §0, then follow its links — do not merge docs.

Also read before implementing:

- [`docs/SLICES_PLAN_CLOUD.md`](../../docs/SLICES_PLAN_CLOUD.md) — slice status & TDD gate
- [`PROJECT_RULES.md`](../../PROJECT_RULES.md) — DX: TDD, layers, code standards (line limits), UI
- [`AGENTS_CLOUD.md`](../../AGENTS_CLOUD.md) — stack, commands, key files
- [`docs/OWASP_MOBILE_TOP_10.md`](../../docs/OWASP_MOBILE_TOP_10.md) — before auth/storage/crypto/network/logging (keep as-is)

**On-device historical:** [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) + [`docs/SLICES_PLAN.md`](../../docs/SLICES_PLAN.md) + [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).

Quick enforcers:

- Slice: `IN PROGRESS` + test plan before code; `DONE` only when tests green
- Layers: `app/` → `stores/` → `services/` — no native/provider calls from screens
- No PHI in logs; provider secrets only on server / env
- Cloud: no LangChain; STT/LLM behind adapters; server-side recording
- iOS + Android; web is UI/dev only unless a cloud slice says otherwise

File-scoped detail: `typescript-standards.mdc`, `react-native-ui.mdc`, `navigation.mdc`. On-device ExecuTorch memory rules (`ai-pipeline.mdc`) apply only to on-device work.

Skills: `.ai/skills/` — canonical cloud docs beat skills when they conflict. Canonical docs: `ARCHITECTURE_CLOUD.md`, `SLICES_PLAN_CLOUD.md`, `PROJECT_RULES.md`, `OWASP_MOBILE_TOP_10.md`.
